# =====================================================================
# ACTOM QGrid — Inspections
#
# NOTE ON config.js — read before changing this.
#
# The Apprenticeship Portal commits apps/*/config.js deliberately, because
# it has ONE Supabase project and no build step to inject the file.
#
# QGrid is different, and the difference is the whole deployment model:
# one database and one Netlify site PER DIVISION, all running the same
# commit. A committed config.js could only ever name one division's
# project, so it must be generated per site instead. That is what
# scripts/gen-config.mjs does, and it is why there IS a build command in
# an otherwise no-build-step project.
#
# The anon key it writes is public by design and appears in every browser
# that loads the app. Every access decision is made by RLS and the
# triggers in db/, not by keeping that key secret.
#
# What must NEVER be committed is the service_role key, the database
# password, and any connection string. Those live in the ACTOM password
# vault and in GitHub Actions secrets. The pre-commit hook in .githooks/
# blocks them, and test-security.js fails the build if one lands anyway.
# =====================================================================

# Generated per site at deploy time
apps/*/config.js
apps/*/_headers

# Secrets — never
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets.json
service-role*
**/service_role*

# Local database harness
/tmp/
pgdata/
*.log

# Tooling
node_modules/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Netlify
.netlify/

# Packaging
*.zip
dist/
